# ztd environment template: user secrets and user-specific endpoints only.
#
#   cp .env.example .env && chmod 600 .env
#
# Every ./ztd command loads ./.env from the working directory (the repo root)
# at startup. The file must be owned by you (or root) with mode 0600 or 0400,
# or ztd refuses to start. Lines are KEY=VALUE (a leading "export " and one
# pair of surrounding quotes are accepted); blank lines and # comments are
# skipped. A variable already exported in the shell wins over the file.
#
# Only the secret and user_endpoint keys in protocol/constants/env_vars.json
# (INV-ENV-04, docs/devs/devs.md) are accepted; any other key is an error. Each
# one is listed below as a commented entry with its purpose, its consumer,
# whether the default flow needs it, and an example value
# (`make constants-check` enforces this). Uncomment and set the ones you need.
# No key is required for the default flow (make up, make gw, make operator,
# ./ztd ...). Secret keys are withheld from governed child processes
# (constants.SecretEnvVars).
#
# Platform configuration (ports, listen host, service URLs, passkey and CORS
# origins, consensus, doctrine and vault paths, models) is never an env
# setting: it is a typed default or a flag (`./ztd <command> --help`). Provider
# API keys and web search are configured in platform settings. The master key
# is selected with --master-key-file.

# =============================================================================
# Inference (optional)
# =============================================================================
# Purpose: Approved Ollama provider endpoint when it is not on this host (default http://127.0.0.1:11434); --inference-ollama-endpoint overrides it.
# Consumer: ./ztd gw start, ./ztd operator start, ./ztd operator model commands (make up, make gw, make operator).
# Required for default flow: no
# ZTD_OLLAMA_ENDPOINT=http://192.168.1.10:11434

# =============================================================================
# Cloudflare (optional)
# =============================================================================
# Purpose: Cloudflare API token with DNS edit permission on the zone that routes the tunnel hostname; --api-token overrides it.
# Consumer: ./ztd gw tunnel route-dns (docs/guides/cloudflare_tunnel.md).
# Required for default flow: no
# CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN=your-cloudflare-api-token
